  "README.md": "KEE Diagnostic and Visualization Tool\n\n## Overview\nThe KEE (Knowledge Expression Language) Diagnostic and Visualization Tool is a specialized utility designed for analyzing Knowledge Base (KB) structures. It provides real-time visualization of semantic networks, dependency tracking, and diagnostic reporting for KEE-compliant systems.\n\n## Features\n- **Semantic Network Visualization**: Renders KEE ontologies as interactive graphs.\n- **Diagnostic Reporting**: Identifies isolated concepts, circular dependencies, and orphaned links.\n- **KB Health Monitoring**: Calculates structural metrics for knowledge base integrity.\n- **Real-time Analysis**: Instant feedback on KB modifications.\n\n## Usage\nLoad a KEE knowledge base file and run the diagnostic engine:\n```kee\nkee-diagnostics --load my_kb.kee --verbose --graphviz --health-report\n```\n\n## Architecture\n- `main.kee`: Entry point and core analysis engine.\n- `visualizer.kee`: Graph rendering and network topology analysis.\n- `diagnostics.kee`: Rule-based diagnostic checks.\n- `health_metrics.kee`: Statistical and structural health monitoring.\n\n## Dependencies\n- KEE Runtime Environment v3.2+\n- Graphviz (for visualization output)\n- Standard KEE libraries\n\n## License\nMIT License\n"
